1
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:08,868
On the Routing card, Default priority decides which waiting items are offered first.

2
00:00:08,868 --> 00:00:10,600
Normal is the default.

3
00:00:11,152 --> 00:00:13,900
Routing strategy picks the next agent.

4
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:18,085
Longest idle is the agent who has been available the longest.

5
00:00:18,085 --> 00:00:21,770
Round robin is the agent who least recently got work.

6
00:00:21,770 --> 00:00:25,892
Least busy is the agent with the fewest active interactions.

7
00:00:26,407 --> 00:00:31,192
Prefer the last assigned agent offers a returning customer to the agent they

8
00:00:31,192 --> 00:00:34,227
spoke to before, when that agent is available.

9
00:00:34,887 --> 00:00:40,166
Reservation timeout is how many seconds an offer rings for one agent.

10
00:00:40,166 --> 00:00:43,897
Unanswered offer action says what happens next:

11
00:00:43,897 --> 00:00:47,347
Requeue, Send to voicemail, or Reject call.

